title: "rfm-pipeline: A Python package for reduced-form modeling pipelines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hettinger
    given-names: Dylan
    email: dylan.hettinger@nlr.gov
    affiliation: National Renewable Energy Laboratory
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/rfm-pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/rfm-pipeline"
abstract: >-
  rfm-pipeline is a Python package for building and executing reduced-form
  modeling (RFM) pipelines on large-scale simulation or observational datasets.
  It provides empirical-null screening, interaction discovery, nonlinear
  discovery, sparse selection with stability filtering, and final manuscript
  table and figure generation. The package supports both local execution and
  distributed SLURM array job workflows for HPC environments.
